## Setup

Let $a_{i,j}$ be the number of sun symbols on tile $(i,j)$, and let $S_{i,j} = \sum_{r=1}^{i}\sum_{c=1}^{j} a_{r,c}$ be the prefix sum (sum of the entire $i\times j$ northwest rectangle).

**Rules:**
- $a_{1,j} = 1$ and $a_{i,1} = 1$ for all $i,j$.
- For $i,j \ge 2$: $a_{i,j} = S_{i-1,\,j-1}$.

**Key observation:** Since $a_{i,j} = S_{i-1,j-1}$, the prefix sum satisfies
$$S_{i,j} = S_{i-1,j} + S_{i,j-1} - S_{i-1,j-1} + a_{i,j} = S_{i-1,j} + S_{i,j-1},$$
i.e., $S$ obeys Pascal's recurrence, with boundaries $S_{1,j}=j$ and $S_{i,1}=i$.

